    "name": "MeArm Pocket Robot Arm",
    "function": "A pocket-sized four-axis robot arm: SG90 servos turn the base, lift the shoulder, bend the elbow and close the claw, and an Arduino Nano plays back recorded pick-and-place moves, from four AA cells in the base.",
    "quote": "Let's build a MeArm, the pocket-sized robot arm: four SG90 servos for the base, shoulder, elbow and claw, an Arduino Nano that plays back pick-and-place moves, and four AA batteries in the base. Under 40 euros and 400 grams. Stretched all the way out with a 20 gram sweet in the claw, the shoulder servo needs 1.5 times the torque, the forearm must not sag more than half a millimetre, and the base must not tip. It should run an hour of demos on one set of batteries.",
